Command Line - Also called as the Command Line Interface(CLT) or Terminal.
The command line is a program where you type commands to perform tasks such as creating files, running programs,
navigating folders, and managing your system.
The four basic command line functionalities are Navigation, Manipulation, Redirection, Configuration.
Navigation - Move around the file system.
Manipulation - Manage files and directories.
Redirection - Control where command input and output go.
Configuration - Set up the shell environment and environment variables.
For windows - Command Prompt
For MacOS/Linus - Bash
